394-//
395-// The four probes above are INSTANTANEOUS — they say what is true right now and
396-// keep no memory. Everything below turns that into history: the worker monitor
397-// calls sampleHealth() on its cadence to persist one HealthSample per component,
398-// and the readers compute uptime %, a bucketed timeline, and open/resolved
399-// incidents from those rows. All the arithmetic is factored into PURE functions
400-// (uptimeFromSamples / bucketTimeline / decideIncident) so it is unit-testable
401-// with an injected clock and injected samples, no DB required.
